type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Dealing With Customers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you deal with customers in a restaurant, you or the customer may ask for information or provide information.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Generally when you ask for or provide information in a formal situation (customer to waiter), you use modals like <span class=\"italic\">can, could, will</span> and  <span class=\"italic\">would</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you are speaking to someone you know well (customer to customer), you are less formal and ask and answer questions more directly.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"More Formal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Less Formal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Waiter</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Are you sure you wouldn't like to look at the specials?</span><br/>   <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Customer</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">No thank you. I wouldn't.</span><br/><br/><br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Waiter</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">How would you like your filets cooked?</span><br/>  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Customer</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll have mine well done.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Miranda</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Don't you think that's extravagant, Edmund?</span><br/>   <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Edmund</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Nothing is too good for you, Miranda!</span> <br/><br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Miranda</span>:<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Are you sure, Edmund? A little bread is good with wine.</span><br/> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Edmund</span>: <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Oh fine. Let's have rolls.</span><br/> (this response is slightly impolite)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Making Polite Requests and Responding to Polite Requests", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you make polite requests, you use modals like: <span class=\"italic\">can, could, will,</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you respond to requests, you can use future tenses like <span class=\"italic\">will, going to, the Present Simple</span> and <span class=\"italic\">the Present Continuous</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Make a Request\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Respond to a Request\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can I get sour cream with the potatoes?<span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Yes, <span class=\\\"strong\\\">we're serving</span> them with sour cream and chives.</span>  (Present Continuous)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'd also like the salad dressing on the side.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">That's not <span class=\\\"strong\\\">going to</span> be a problem. </span>  (Going to)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We'll have this Merlot with the steak.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">I'll</span> see if we have a bottle of that left.</span>  (Will)<br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Our wine delivery <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is</span> tomorrow.</span>  (Present Simple)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Would you like to keep the menus or can I take them?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm <span class=\\\"strong\\\">going to</span> have a look at the desserts, so please leave one.</span>  (Going to)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can I offer you a basket?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">No, thanks, we're not having rolls.</span>  (Present Continuous)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "well done", "type": "name"}, {"content": "meat that is cooked thoroughly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll have my steak well done.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to order food.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sour cream", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a dairy product; fermented cream", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Is there sour cream for the baked potatoes?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "on the side", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not on the plate or on top of the food", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Could I have my salad dressing on the side?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "filet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a premium cut of beef", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We'd both like filet steaks, please.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Merlot", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a type of red wine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We'll have some Merlot wine with our dinner.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "roll", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small crusty bread", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are small rolls this week to go with dinner.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rare", "type": "name"}, {"content": "cooked to be pink or bloody inside", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I prefer my steak rare.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "salad dressing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a thick liquid to put on salad greens", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Can I have some salad dressing, please?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Find an American restaurant online and look at the menu.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a dialogue asking a friend to come with you to the restaurant. (be polite and use modals)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use future tenses to say which dishes you are going to try. Ask what your friend is going to try on the menu.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the dialogue aloud with a partner. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change roles and read it again.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look at food and drink in a restaurant menu.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a request. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about food and drink I am going to have.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for information.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn8le02ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn8le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn8le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Are you sure you wouldn't like to look at the daily specials?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Melinda</span>: No thank you. This is Edmund's favorite meal!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: How would you like your filets cooked?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Edmund </span>: I'll have mine well done.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Melinda</span>: I'm going to have mine rare. Are you serving sour cream with the potatoes?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I can arrange that.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn8le02ob03re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Melinda</span>: I'd also like the salad dressing on the side.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Of course. That's not a problem.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Edmund </span>: We'll  have another bottle of wine as well, please.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Melinda</span>: Are you sure Edmund? It seems so extravagant!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Edmund </span>: Nothing is too good for you Melinda!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Would you like the same wine, sir?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Edmund </span>: No. We'll have this Merlot with the steak.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\